# mental map — a full memory forgets its oldest unlocked map, never a locked one
#
# One anamnesis point holds four mental maps. The first place is visited and its map locked; four
# more are visited. The fifth needs a slot: the oldest map is the locked one, so the second place's
# map is forgotten in its stead. Four remembered at the end, and the locked map among them.
#
# Every place is the test location (--location-type test), visited and left at once: arriving is
# what makes a map.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --organs anamnesis=1

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

expect-state mental-maps mental-maps used=1 usable=4
manage Chorography lock oldest
wait 10
expect ☑
manage
wait mode WorldView 30
expect-state mental-maps locked=yes

# Three more: the memory is full.
travel new
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

travel new
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

travel new
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90
expect-state mental-maps mental-maps used=4

# A fifth: the second place is forgotten, not the locked first.
travel new
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90
expect-state mental-maps mental-maps used=4
expect-state mental-maps locked=yes
save roundtrip
quit
